      },
      {
        "id": "253e7fc5-b914-4c7b-aacf-fad12bf82f83",
        "name": "Sorter Notes",
        "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
        "typeVersion": 1,
        "position": [
          0,
          -160
        ],
        "parameters": {
          "color": 4,
          "width": 1700,
          "height": 300,
          "content": "## Sorter (C2, oneshotllc/.github#29)\n\nThe only place routing lives. Every minute: load `automation/streams.json` from oneshotllc/.github once, then loop RPOP `queue:intake` (max 500 per run): drop anything whose `seen:{owner}/{repo}#{n}` claim already exists, otherwise look up repo → stream in the table and LPUSH to `queue:<stream>` with `stream` set in the payload.\n\nNo model calls here, ever. If a rule needs judgment it belongs in triage. Consumers read `queue:<stream>` only and reject items without `stream`. The consumer's INCR claim stays the atomic first-winner guard; the EXISTS check here only stops already-handled items from re-entering a stream queue."
        }
      }
